    "memo": " BILL NUMBER:  S4364A\n\n TITLE OF BILL :\nAn act to amend the not-for-profit corporation law, in relation to the\nmaintenance, protection and preservation of abandoned cemeteries\n\n\n PURPOSE: :\nThis bill would allow solvent cemetery corporations the ability to\nassume management and maintenance of abandoned cemeteries and thereby\nprevent them from becoming the responsibility of the taxpayers of the\nmunicipalities in which they are located.\n\n SUMMARY OF PROVISIONS: :\nThis bill adds a new section 1506-b to the not-for-profit corporation\nlaw to outline the process and requirements for a solvent cemetery\ncorporation to assume management and maintenance of an abandoned\ncemetery.\n\nThe provisions of this section outline exactly what monies may be used\nfor in restoration of the abandoned cemetery. This section\nadditionally requires any unused funds be returned to the New York\nState Cemetery Board to be returned to the abandoned cemetery fund.\n\nSection 2 amends section 1507 of the not-for-profit corporation law to\nauthorize payments from the state abandoned cemetery fund.\n\n EXISTING LAW: :\nExisting law provides for maintenance and preservation of abandoned\ncemeteries but does not allow the incentive for solvent cemetery\ncorporations to apply to the state fund to save these abandoned\ncemeteries.\n\n JUSTIFICATION: :\nMany municipalities are in no condition to assume the maintenance and\npreservation of an abandoned cemetery corporation.  The added fiscal\nburden to localities is often more than they can handle.  The result\nis many cemeteries do not receive the care necessary to revitalize\nthem or to stop decay and vandalism.\n\nThis legislation would allow cemetery corporations the ability to\napply to the state abandoned cemetery fund, and upon approval by the\nState Cemetery Board, assume the maintenance and preservation of these\ngrounds.\n\nExisting cemetery corporations have the knowledge and staff to better\nhandle the upkeep and operation of these entities. Additionally, the\ncare of these cemeteries prevents the fiscal burden of cemetery\nmaintenance from being applied to municipalities.\n\n LEGISLATIVE HISTORY: :\nA.6209-A (2005-06)\nA.1329 (2007-08)\n\n FISCAL IMPLICATIONS: :\nNone. cemeteries contribute to a fund created under section 97-r of\nthe state finance law for the maintenance of abandoned cemeteries. The\nfund is financed by contributions from cemeteries on a per interment\nor cremation basis.\n\n EFFECTIVE DATE: :\nThis act shall take effect on the sixtieth day after it shall have\nbecome law.\n\n\n\n",
